The optional architecture to use, e.g.
.Ar arm64 .
.El
.It Li visionOS Simulator
A simulated visionOS device, which supports the following keys:
.Bl -tag -width "name"
.It Ar id
The identifier of the simulated device to use, as shown in the Devices window. A valid destination specifier must provide either
.Ar id
or
.Ar name ,
but not both.
.It Ar name
The name of the simulated device to use. A valid destination specifier must provide either
.Ar id
or
.Ar name ,
but not both.
.It Ar OS
When specifying the simulated device by
.Ar name ,
the visionOS version for that simulated device, such as
.Ar 3.0 ,
or the string
.Ar latest
.Pq the default
to indicate the most recent version of visionOS supported by this version of Xcode.
.El
.It Li DriverKit
The DriverKit environment, which supports the following key:
.Bl -tag -width "arch"
.It Ar arch
The optional architecture to use, e.g.
.Ar arm64
or
.Ar x86_64 .
.El
.Pp
Some actions (such as building) may be performed without an actual device present.
To build against a platform generically instead of a specific device, the destination specifier may be prefixed with the optional string "generic/", indicating that the platform should be targeted generically.
An example of a generic destination is the "Any iOS Device" destination displayed in Xcode's UI when no physical iOS device is present.
.Pp
.\"
.Ss Testing on Multiple Destinations
When more than one destination is specified with the
.Fl destination
option,
.Nm
tests on those destinations concurrently. In this mode,
.Nm
automatically chooses the number of devices and simulators that are used simultaneously. All enabled tests in the scheme or xctestrun file are run on each destination.
.Pp
.\"
.Ss Distributing Archives
The
.Fl exportArchive
option specifies that
.Nm
should distribute the archive specified by
.Fl archivePath
using the options specified by
.Fl exportOptionsPlist .
.Nm
.Fl help
can print the full set of available inputs to
.Fl exportOptionsPlist .
The product can either be uploaded to Apple or exported locally. The exported product will be placed at the path specified by
.Fl exportPath .
.Pp
Archives that have been uploaded to the Apple notary service can be distributed using the
.Fl exportNotarizedApp
option. This specifies that
.Nm
should export a notarized app from the archive specified by
.Fl archivePath
and place the exported product at the path specified by
.Fl exportPath .
If the archive has not completed processing by the notary service, or processing failed, then
.Nm
will exit and emit informational or error messages.
.Pp
When uploading an archive using the
.Fl exportArchive
option, or exporting a notarized archive using the
.Fl exportNotarizedApp
option, an Apple ID account belonging to the archive's development team is required. Enter the credentials for the Apple ID account using Xcode's Accounts preference pane before invoking
.Nm .
.\"
.Ss Environment Variables
The following environment variables affect the execution of
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev CLICOLOR_FORCE"
.It Ev XCODE_XCCONFIG_FILE
Set to a path to a file, build settings in that file will be loaded and used when building all targets.  These settings will override all other settings, including settings passed individually on the command line, and those in the file passed with the
.Fl xcconfig
option.
.El
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev CLICOLOR_FORCE"
.It Ev TEST_RUNNER_<VAR>
Set an environment variable whose name is prefixed with
.Sy TEST_RUNNER_
to have that variable passed, with its prefix stripped, to all test runner processes launched during a test action. For example,
.Sy TEST_RUNNER_Foo=Bar xcodebuild test ...
sets the environment variable
.Sy Foo=Bar
in the test runner's environment. Existing variables may be modified using the special token
.Sy __CURRENT_VALUE__
to represent their current value. For example,
.Sy TEST_RUNNER_Foo=__CURRENT_VALUE__:Bar
appends the string
.Sy :Bar
to any existing value of
.Sy Foo .
.El
.Ss Exit Codes
.Nm
exits with codes defined by
.Xr sysexits 3 .
It will exit with
.Sy EX_OK
on success.  On failure, it will commonly exit with
.Sy EX_USAGE
if any options appear malformed,
.Sy EX_NOINPUT
if any input files cannot be found,
.Sy EX_IOERR
if any files cannot be read or written, and
.Sy EX_SOFTWARE
if the commands given to xcodebuild fail.  It may exit with other codes in less common scenarios.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width -indent
.It Li "xcodebuild clean install"
.Pp
Cleans the build directory; then builds and installs the first target in the Xcode project in the directory from which
.Nm
was started.
.Pp
.\"
.It Li "xcodebuild -project MyProject.xcodeproj -target Target1 -target Target2 -configuration Debug"
.Pp
Builds the targets 
.Em Target1
and
.Em Target2
in the project
.Em MyProject.xcodeproj
using the
.Em Debug
configuration.
.\"
.It Li "xcodebuild -target MyTarget OBJROOT=/Build/MyProj/Obj.root SYMROOT=/Build/MyProj/Sym.root"
.Pp
Builds the target 
.Em MyTarget
in the Xcode project in the directory from which
.Nm
was started, putting intermediate files in the directory
.Ar /Build/MyProj/Obj.root
and the products of the build in the directory
.Ar /Build/MyProj/Sym.root .
.\"
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild -sdk macosx10.6"
.Pp
Builds the Xcode project in the directory from which
.Nm
was started against the macOS 10.6 SDK.  The canonical names of all available SDKs can be viewed using the
.Fl showsdks
option.
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild -workspace MyWorkspace.xcworkspace -scheme MyScheme"
.Pp
Builds the scheme
.Ar MyScheme
in the Xcode workspace
.Ar MyWorkspace.xcworkspace .
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild archive -workspace MyWorkspace.xcworkspace -scheme MyScheme"
.Pp
Archives the scheme
.Ar MyScheme
in the Xcode workspace
.Ar MyWorkspace.xcworkspace .
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild build-for-testing -workspace MyWorkspace.xcworkspace -scheme MyScheme -destination generic/platform=iOS"
.Pp
Build tests and associated targets in the scheme
.Ar MyScheme
in the Xcode workspace
.Ar MyWorkspace.xcworkspace
using the generic iOS device destination. The command also writes test parameters from the scheme to an xctestrun file in the built products directory.
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild test-without-building -workspace MyWorkspace.xcworkspace -scheme MyScheme -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 5s' -destination 'platform=iOS,name=My iPad'"
.Pp
Tests the scheme
.Ar MyScheme
in the Xcode workspace
.Ar MyWorkspace.xcworkspace
using both the iOS Simulator and the device named
.Ar iPhone 5s
for the latest version of iOS. The command assumes the test bundles are in the build root
.Pq SYMROOT .
(Note that the shell requires arguments to be quoted or otherwise escaped if they contain spaces.)
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild test-without-building -xctestrun MyTestRun.xctestrun -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 5s' -destination 'platform=iOS,name=My iPad' "
.Pp
Tests using both the iOS Simulator and the device named
.Ar iPhone 5s .
Test bundle paths and other test parameters are specified in
.Ar MyTestRun.xctestrun .
The command requires project binaries and does not require project source code.
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild test -workspace MyWorkspace.xcworkspace -scheme MyScheme -destination 'platform=macOS,arch=x86_64'"
.Pp
Tests the scheme
.Ar MyScheme
in the Xcode workspace
.Ar MyWorkspace.xcworkspace
using the destination described as
.Ar "My Mac 64-bit"
in Xcode.
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild test -workspace MyWorkspace.xcworkspace -scheme MyScheme -destination 'platform=macOS,arch=x86_64' -only-testing MyTests/FooTests/testFooWithBar"
.Pp
Tests the scheme
.Ar MyScheme
in the Xcode workspace
.Ar MyWorkspace.xcworkspace
using the destination described as
.Ar My Mac 64-bit
in Xcode. Only the test
.Ar testFooWithBar
of the test suite
.Ar FooTests,
part of the
.Ar MyTests
testing bundle target, will be run.
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild -exportArchive -archivePath MyMobileApp.xcarchive -exportPath ExportDestination -exportOptionsPlist 'export.plist'"
.Pp
Exports the archive
.Ar MyMobileApp.xcarchive
to the path
.Ar ExportDestination
using the options specified in
.Ar "export.plist" .
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild -exportLocalizations -project MyProject.xcodeproj -localizationPath MyDirectory -exportLanguage zh-hans -exportLanguage es-MX"
.Pp
Exports two XLIFF files to
.Ar MyDirectory
from
.Ar MyProject.xcodeproj
containing development language strings and translations for Simplified Chinese and Mexican Spanish.
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild -exportLocalizations -project MyProject.xcodeproj -localizationPath MyDirectory
.Pp
Export a single XLIFF file to
.Ar MyDirectory
from
.Ar MyProject.xcodeproj
containing only development language strings. (In this case, the
.Fl exportLanguage
parameter has been excluded.)
.Pp
.It Li "xcodebuild -importLocalizations -project MyProject.xcodeproj -localizationPath MyLocalizations.xliff
.Pp
Imports localizations from
.Ar MyLocalizations.xliff
into
.Ar MyProject.xcodeproj .
Translations with issues will be reported but not imported.
.El
